One thing I would change

I would not store the SharePoint logic mixed into your existing AddMakeVsBuyView() method.

Instead:

Save Estimate

↓

MbNumber generated

↓

Popup gets MbNumber

↓

Separate UploadDocuments() endpoint

That separation is valuable because:

Saving an estimate shouldn't fail because SharePoint is temporarily unavailable.
Users can add documents later.
Users can delete or replace documents independently.
The code stays easier to maintain.
My recommendation for your project

Based on your existing codebase, I would use:

✅ Dapper directly in the controller
✅ Graph SDK called directly from the controller (or a small helper class)
✅ No Repository pattern
✅ No Service layer
✅ No MediatR
✅ No Unit of Work
✅ One new SQL table (SBCES.MBDocument)
✅ Telerik Upload + Telerik Grid in the popup

This fits the style of the rest of your application while remaining production-ready and avoiding unnecessary complexity.
